# Typography

One job per family. Never mix two families inside one role.

| Family | Font | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| Serif (`font-serif`) | Gelasio | Headlines: every `h1`–`h3`, dialog titles, the footer wordmark, the closing "Hiring?" line |
| Sans (`font-sans`, default) | Geist | Everything read or operated: body, subtitles, pull lines, nav, buttons, card titles, form fields |
| Mono (`font-mono`) | Geist Mono | Small metadata labels (uppercase, tracked) |

- Headlines are `font-serif font-normal` (Gelasio ships one weight; never `font-medium`/`font-semibold` on it) with tracking around `-0.025em`.
- An emphasis word inside a headline is `<em className="text-brand">` — same family, italic, brand green. No size bump, no family switch.
- Never put `font-serif` on a paragraph, subtitle, link or button.
- Sans headings are not allowed; a title that needs weight contrast should change size, not family.
